✔ A grenadier announces a real ballistic throw, keeps its committed aim and gives enough time to leave the blast (27.019958ms)
✔ A rocketeer refuses an ally inside the blast area, then launches once the ally leaves (25.529959ms)
✔ Grenade trajectories respect a low ceiling even when the bot repositions for a lower arc (31.918875ms)
✔ A punctured pipe warns before hot gas, hurts at its actual nozzle and can be escaped or blocked by cover (76.885041ms)
✔ A pressure plate announces spikes and allows retreat; a press stops at the body instead of clipping through it (115.459584ms)
✔ A moving blade stops at physical contact and restores its actual stopped pose (80.414333ms)
✔ Destruction checkpoints retain flying explosives and leaking machinery; corrupted changes fail atomically (185.819041ms)
✔ Fallback outdoor substrate never overrides a higher ramp or terrace (20.327083ms)
✔ ground() answers exactly like a scan of its 8 m bucket, on floor edges, cell borders and odd values (2629.0885ms)
✔ ground() follows the floor list and the trap list it reads, including restored traps (127.391125ms)
✔ A real rocket knocks the player off a terrace and falling onto the deep substrate is fatal (16.330125ms)
✔ The actual three generated arenas cannot strand the player after a blast-sized shove through a destroyed rail (2130.848791ms)
✔ An already invalid player below terrain dies despite recovery and dash (13.288542ms)
✔ A grounded checkpoint on a collider underneath terrain is rejected without changing the live game (3.460584ms)
✔ Breached ground-level exterior, ordinary lower floors and space beneath raised props stay safe (36.867958ms)
✔ Each giant has its real size and health, remains dormant outside the arena, and physically blocks passage (1599.23575ms)
✔ A giant slam announces the exact danger area, can be escaped, and exposes the visible core for stronger aimed damage (566.57ms)
✔ Giant phases release only the six physically preplaced reinforcements, retain IDs, and clamp the entire silhouette to its arena (582.675166ms)
✔ The three giant scripts produce distinct physical attacks and real cannon rockets instead of damage-only visual effects (1778.219333ms)
✔ Giant helmets, legs and exposed cores are targetable at their scaled positions while opaque walls still occlude them (680.280458ms)
✔ A giant encounter restores telegraphs, projectiles, phases and reserves exactly, rejects corrupted scripts and saves its real death (846.382625ms)
✔ The first-sector entry has ten real seconds of grace, then observable enemies resume normal announced attacks (48.303167ms)
✔ Difficulty changes real hostile cadence, projectile speed and damage while preserving enemy health and actor count (123.173333ms)
✔ Horror events use fixed physical sites; an ambush follows the audible site without discovering a hidden player (16.045208ms)
✔ Director pressure, difficulty and event timing round-trip exactly and malformed horror saves fail atomically (63.186292ms)
✔ A breach changes collision immediately; the walking map follows it locally in bounded batches, and a change beyond a quarter of the grid stays amortised (1972.891291ms)
✔ After several breaches and a door opening, the walking map and every cached edge at rest equal a full rebuild (164.369708ms)
✔ A door opened by progression updates the walking map beside it as soon as it clears a body, matching a full rebuild at every step (1287.859ms)
✔ Route tests and cached edges read the static map only; a moving blade still blocks bodies (SIM-V1) (67.267ms)
✔ Periodic pipe bursts spare their physical source, but external destruction ends future autonomous bursts (85.6975ms)
✔ a shot severs a real rail which falls, collides, bounces and persists in a coherent settled pose (107.542208ms)
✔ persistent wreckage restores exactly in flight and at rest, while corrupt rubble checkpoints fail atomically (295.131417ms)
✔ an actual breached wall keeps substantial rubble after landing without adding player collision blockers (82.983875ms)
✔ a destroyed sliding gate becomes actual metal plates, retains its volume, and restores after settling (74.813166ms)
✔ detached hollow hardware lands on its rendered torus instead of hovering on an invisible filled box (168.97025ms)
✔ settled wreckage wakes and falls when its real supporting platform is destroyed (74.164792ms)
✔ a demolition storm has a finite rubble budget and cannot retire settled wreckage at the player’s feet (624.712916ms)
